            <div class="alert alert-info mt-4">
                <h2 class="h4 fw-bold">Summary</h2>

                <p class="mb-0">
                    HTML form attributes control how forms submit and handle data.
                    The most important attributes include <code>action</code>,
                    <code>method</code>, <code>target</code>,
                    <code>autocomplete</code>, <code>enctype</code>,
                    <code>novalidate</code>, and <code>accept-charset</code>.
                    <code>GET</code> is commonly used for query-style operations,
                    while <code>POST</code> sends form data in the request body.
                    For file uploads, <code>multipart/form-data</code> is commonly
                    used.
                </p>
